    note: `If PayTabs checkout is part of a new store, it is inside the store price from ${P.shop} and not billed separately. Adding it to an existing custom site is quoted after we read your order code, because the cost sits in how your current order states, refunds and emails are written rather than in the gateway calls themselves. A maintained cart plugin plus a configuration and hardening pass is a small job and we quote it as one. Subscriptions, an agreement record you can defend, a customer-facing billing portal and dunning are custom work from ${P.software}, and in-app checkout inside a new app starts from ${P.app}. What genuinely moves the number is the dispute-evidence work, the settlement tracing and whether you need a second country profile — those are the three lines clients most often underestimate. PayTabs' own charges are paid to PayTabs and never pass through our invoice; our build-side figures are on <a href='/pricing/'>our pricing page</a>.`,
